  "coverageNote": "25 purpose-scoped owners in seven disjoint installation bundles. pstack (cursor/plugins/pstack) is the assumed engineering workflow, so skills that overlapped it (discovery, verification, design, delivery, review, debugging, testing, refactoring, Git submission, onboarding, security review, hc delegation, writing, research and document review) are archived under archive/skills/. Evidence and research standards live in the owner's global AGENTS.md instead. The remaining engineering, interface-review and data skills are project-local. Workstation, Linux, macOS and agent-tooling bundles are optional global specialists. Selective activation is not a mandatory workflow graph. All entrypoints share a word bound. CLI-managed herdr-core/ketch are excluded. Source changes do not modify live installations or immutable npm releases.",
